{{Quote|Collectors should keep an eye out for statues of the Four Sages of Dwartii&mdash;Sistros, Braata, Faya, and Yanjun ''[sic]''&mdash;the ancient philosophers and lawmakers who influenced the earliest laws in the Galactic Republic.|Eloc Throno, ''Traveler's Guide to Batuu''|<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref>}}
'''Yanjon Zelmar''' was a member of the [[Four Sages of Dwartii]], controversial lawgiver-[[philosopher]]s who influenced the [[Galactic Republic]]'s early laws. A [[19 BBY|millennium after]] the founding of the Republic, a [[bronzium]] statue of Zelmar stood outside the door to [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine's]] [[Emperor's office|private office]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Yanjon Zelmar is depicted wearing a regal headdress and reaching inside one sleeve, as if seeking to locate some treasure or seize a weapon.|A book's description of Yanjon Zelmar's statue|<ref name="100 Objects">''[[Star Wars 100 Objects]]''</ref>}}
Yanjon Zelmar<ref name="Den of Antiquities">{{GEAttr|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref> was one of the controversial [[Four Sages of Dwartii]], ancient lawgivers and [[philosopher]]s from the [[planet]] [[Dwartii]] in the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]].<ref name="Inside Intel" /> After the [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] was ousted from the<ref name="Propaganda">''[[Star Wars Propaganda: A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]''</ref> [[The galaxy|galactic]]<ref name="Timelines" /> [[capital]] of [[Coruscant]]<ref name="Propaganda" /> and the [[Sith]] Order [[Era of the Sith|reigned]] over the [[galaxy]], statues were made of Zelmar and the other Sages: [[Sistros Nevet]], [[Braata Danlos]], and [[Faya Rodemos]].<ref name="Den of Antiquities" /> The Republic, aided by the [[Jedi Order]], [[Jedi-Sith War|defeated]] the Sith<ref name="Propaganda" /> in [[1032 BBY]], marking what was believed to be the latter's extinction.<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

[[File:FayaYanjon_office.png|thumb|left|310px|Statues of Yanjon Zelmar and Faya Rodemos were kept outside the private office of Chancellor Palpatine.]]
As a result of their decisive victory, the Republic not only returned to power on Coruscant and made it their capital once more, but also re-formed into the Galactic Republic<ref name="Propaganda" /> that same [[Standard year|year]].<ref name="Timelines" /> The Four Sages, Zelmar included, influenced the [[politics]] of the early Galactic Republic<ref name="Inside Intel" /> and its first laws,<ref name="TVE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> eventually coming to be regarded as having been controversial lawmakers with contentious views.<ref name="100 Objects" /> Republic [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]&mdash;in truth the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Darth]] Sidious&mdash;had large [[bronzium]] statues of both Zelmar and Faya Rodemos positioned on either side of the door to his [[Emperor's office|private office]] on Coruscant<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> by [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Date 2">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|III}}, which includes the appearance of Yanjon Zelmar's statue, to [[19 BBY]].</ref> Slightly smaller statues of the Sages were placed along the hallway to Palpatine's quarters.<ref name="Inside Intel" />

In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="TGDate">{{TravelersGuidetoBatuuDate}}</ref> within his guide [[book]] for the planet [[Batuu]], ''[[Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]'', [[historian]] [[Eloc Throno]] encouraged [[collector]]s to keep an [[eye]] out for<ref name="Traveler's Guide" /> a series of statuettes depicting Zelmar and the other Four Sages of Dwartii possessed by the<ref name="Inside Intel" /> [[Ithorian]] [[antiques dealer]] [[Dok-Ondar]].<ref name="Traveler's Guide" /> The statuettes were put up for sale at Dok-Ondar's shop, the [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities|Den of Antiquities]],<ref name="Inside Intel" /> the same year.<ref name="Date 3">The events of [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities]] within [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]] take place in [[34 ABY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> In both collections, Zelmar's statue showcased the Sage as wearing a hooded [[robe]], over which was a large<ref name="Den of Antiquities" /><ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> headdress.<ref name="100 Objects" /> Details about Zelmar's statue were mentioned in a book looking at the use of [[propaganda]] by various factions, ''[[A History of Persuasive Art in the Galaxy]]'', that was released shortly after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]]<ref name="Propaganda" /> of 34 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]].<ref name="Timelines" /> A [[Unidentified historical book|book]] describing objects relating to [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]] included an entry on statues of the Four Sages of Dwartii, elaborating on how Zelmar's statue was positioned to be reaching inside one sleeve, as if seeking a treasure or reaching for a weapon.<ref name="100 Objects" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Gert [Stevens, concept artist] did two new statues.|Production Designer [[Gavin Bocquet]], on Stevens designing the Yanjon Zelmar and Faya Rodemos statues for ''Revenge of the Sith''|<ref name="Art of Episode III">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode III: Revenge of the Sith]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Faya_Yanjon_statue_concepts.png|thumb|250px|Concept sketches of Yanjon Zelmar and Faya Rodemos' statues by Gert Stevens]]
Yanjon Zelmar first appeared, albeit as a statue, in the [[2005]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']].<ref name="ROTS" /> Sketches of Zelmar's as well as Faya Rodemos' statues were drawn by [[Gert Stevens]], a concept artist for the film.<ref name="Art of Episode III" /> In the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Zelmar's first name was given in the [[2016]] reference book [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']], in a portion detailing locations from ''Revenge of the Sith''.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> [[Kerrie Dougherty]] originally authored that section for the 2005 [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] reference book of the [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2005)|same name]], which also marked the origin of "Yanjon" in Legends.<ref name="Complete Locations 2005">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2005)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'', 2005 edition]]</ref> In both editions of ''Complete Locations'', however, Zelmar's statue is mistakenly identified as being Sistros Nevet's.<ref name="Complete Locations" /><ref name="Complete Locations 2005" />

In [[2019]],<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=creatures-droids-and-aliens-meet-the-fantastical-figures-of-star-wars-galaxys-edge|text=Creatures, Droids, and Aliens: Meet the Fantastical Figures of ''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge}}</ref> the surname "Zelmar" was assigned to Yanjon through the [[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge|''Star Wars'': Galaxy's Edge]]&ndash;themed land<ref name="Den of Antiquities" /> at [[Disneyland]] Park and [[Disney's Hollywood Studios]].<ref name="D23" /> At one of the land's retail locations, Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities, Zelmar's full name is labeled on a box containing small statues of Zelmar and Nevet, which can be purchased by guests.<ref name="Den of Antiquities" /> The [[2020]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]'', written by [[Cole Horton]], misspells Zelmar's first name as "Yanjun."<ref name="Traveler's Guide" />

The non-canon 2019 book ''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Search & Find]]'' depicts a statuette of Zelmar&mdash;alongside other curios&mdash;present at the<ref name="TROS Search & Find">''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Search & Find]]''</ref> [[Forbidden Valley]] of [[Pasaana]]<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref> while [[First Order]] [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] and the [[Knights of Ren]] hunted the [[Resistance]] there<ref name="TROS Search & Find" /> in [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Ren Date">''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Search & Find]]'' depicts [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] searching for the [[Resistance]] on [[Pasaana]], an event also shown in [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']]. ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' places the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' in [[35 ABY]].</ref> during the [[First Order-Resistance War]].<ref name="TROS Search & Find" />

